{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792714996,"nonce":"q5DKhaYqpZCFUY3ipjizOfDC8OA=","title":"Static ancestor groups lose dynamic canvas isolation","message":"Scoped child of e0a7502e3e9d71bb983572df7db0033a67da1c48262e53368ae2399bc22e583a.\n\nDynamic canvas callbacks under static native groups are skipped during the compositor cache paint and collected independently afterward. Their geometry, opacity and command cursors cannot share the ancestor group, so overlap with static siblings loses isolation. Retain same-stream canvas output in its static owner and conservatively request a fresh walk/repaint on subsequent frames; avoid independently collecting or publishing retained canvases as dynamic regions. Preserve unrelated canvas collection and route restoration.\n\nCover native background and foreground groups, changing images/shapes/empty callbacks, clips/auxiliary ownership, nested commands and cache-eligible direct/compositor frames. Keep cross-background/foreground callbacks, independent GPU passes/meshes, separately collected text/SVG/ImageElement, named Sample and general flattening on the parent. CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2 and scoped checks only. Nothing pushed.","files":null}]}